  "whatIsThis": {
    "intro": "An ESC turns battery power into AC signals needed for BLDC motors to spin. This one specifically is sensorless. Do that four times over: per motor a microcontroller running AM32, a gate driver, and six MOSFETs doing the power switching. It listens for throttle commands from the flight controller over DShot and reports motor RPM back on the same wire, which Betaflight uses to filter gyro noise at exactly the motors' frequencies. Current sensing is on board, exposed through the connector to the Flight Controller.",
    "needs": [
      "A flight controller to command it (OpenFC Lite, one 8-pin cable, in the box)",
      "Four brushless motors soldered to the pads",
      "A LiPo on the XT pigtail, with the included low-ESR capacitor across the battery pads",
      "A frame, props, receiver, radio; the usual rest of the drone"
    ],
    "fit": "The layer between the flight controller's digital requests and the raw battery current that actually spins the props.",
    "chain": "esc"
  },
